#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:68
msgid "Configure Backup at Provision Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:70
msgid ""
"When provisioning an Instance into a Cloud where Veeam is set as the "
"backup provider, Veeam will be selectable as the \"Backup Type\" on the "
"Automation tab of the provisioning wizard. Expand the Backups section on "
"this tab and enter the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:72
msgid "**Backup Type:** Select the desired Veeam backup type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:73
msgid ""
"**Repository:** Select a repository synced from the Veeam backup provider"
" associated with the Cloud"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:74
msgid ""
"**Managed Server:** Select a managed server associated with the backup "
"server selected in the previous step"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:75
msgid ""
"**Backup Name:** A name for the backup in Morpheus, this field is pre-"
"populated with the Instance name but can be overwritten"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:76
msgid ""
"**Backup Job Type:** Clone an existing backup job (Backups > Jobs) or add"
" this backup to an existing job. A job contains a retention count and "
"backup frequency schedule and can have as many Instances backing up under"
" it as needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:77
msgid ""
"**Backup Job:** Select the job which will be cloned or have a backup "
"added to it depending on your selection in the prior field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:78
msgid ""
"**Job Name:** A name for the new cloned job (if you are cloning and not "
"creating a new Backup Job)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:80
msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/veeam/2createBackup.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:83
msgid "Viewing Backups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:85
msgid ""
"After provisioning, users can review backup details from the Instance "
"detail page (:menuselection:`Provisioning --> Instances` > Selected "
"Instance > Backups tab). Additionally, backups can be configured here if "
"this was not done during provision time by clicking :guilabel:`ADD "
"BACKUP`. Users can also run one-off backups from this page by opening the"
" ACTIONS menu and clicking Backup. Backups will still continue to run "
"based on the schedule configured in their job but additional runs can be "
"made on-demand this way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:87
msgid ""
"Within the Backups section (Backups > Backups) users can also view all "
"currently-configured backups and whether or not recent backup runs have "
"succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:89
msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/veeam/3viewBackups.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:92
msgid "Restore an Instance from Veeam"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Backups/veeam.rst:94
msgid ""
"For Instances with current backups, the Backup Results section will be "
"populated on the Instance detail page (:menuselection:`Provisioning --> "
"Instances` > Selected Instance > Backup tab). If the Instance needs "
"restored, simply click Actions (within the Backup Results area, not the "
"main actions menu for the Instance itself) and then click Restore. The "
"status icon at the top of the Instance detail page will turn green once "
"this process is finished and the Instance will be fully restored from "
"your selected backup."
msgstr ""

